**Definition (Terminal entry)** · `def:generator:terminal-entry` The first entry act acquires the two named receiver capabilities through (`[SECRETHOME-def:home:named-delivery]`). Successful acquisition is followed by establishment of the exactly two-page protection budget before public parsing and observation can start a worker. The command records the four public convention values without mutating them, constructs one independent password and verifier, attempts both typed deliveries, attempts checked completion of both homes and aggregates every observable result before returning directly to process exit. A construction error is not confirmed cleanup. No private byte, writer or callback enters the executable; the private lifecycle interface carries only content-free stage results. Success reports two locked pages and the two accepted lengths, 64 and 135 bytes; accepted bytes are not a sealing or publication verdict. Standard output carries one public JSON success object and standard error the shared JSON command and observation contract (`[ROOT-rec:output:decision]`). Every runtime refusal returns status one with its fixed public class, including a failure after both full writes; usage returns two and help/version return zero. Destroying a handle confirms no close result. The originals remain open until process exit, and another writer reference can delay end of input thereafter.

**Criterion (Finite generator evidence)** · `crit:generator:evidence` For (`verif:generator:terminal`), (`claim:generator:terminal-driver-checks-every-stage-before-exit`) exercises the production ordering function with 36 distinct public stage-outcome tuples. (`claim:generator:completion-model-requires-the-matching-supervisor-result`) requires the matching ended and successful supervisor record as well as exact ended streams. (`claim:generator:stream-model-keeps-the-complete-calibration-premise`) refuses invalid premises, changed calibration inputs and mismatching sealed lengths. (`claim:generator:process-delivery-keeps-private-streams-out-of-public-output`) executes fresh processes in both name orders, a metadata refusal and a closed reader, counting exact private streams only in an external receiver fixture and checking the public JSON and trace. (`[ROOT-claim:discipline:credential-models-cannot-enter-production]`) checks the closed test source and manifest roster. These controls do not establish the supervisor's record, calibration law, sealing, publication or installation custody. The lifecycle controls exercise the same private stage-ordering function as the production adapter and inject public outcomes, not entropy or protected bytes; owning-package controls establish the protected constructor, writes and checked completion separately. The source census also pins the owning entry's tail return, refusing work appended after the terminal lifecycle. The executable controls retain only public status and stream lengths. The completion and stream models live solely in tests and do not implement external publication. The declared calibration premise has separate fixed-name, content-independence, non-decreasing and lower/upper local-strictness members; each is necessary in the model, which proves none of the installed measure's properties. Their source and manifest census rejects production reachability, exports and feature activation; no model closes an installation premise. Generator timing, locked and scratch observations are reported with the measured process conditions, never used as node-ready or cleanup bounds.

